title The four that stayed home on their merits, and a sweep that rewrote the lift it had just written
prompt Autonomous loop, second lap of the round -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, the queue head named by the lap before it.
think revoke_one was the head at four hundred and sixty-eight, and the lap before named the reading to apply: an import binding is free when the harness already holds the module. Read the private symbols first -- all forty widenings bind cycle, and caravan/ladder_checks.rye imports cycle in its own head. Free before a line was written.
think Read the four that differ before trusting the identity count, since the lap before had just proved a differing body can be structural. All four are: abandon.rye, reckon.rye, reclaim.rye, and revoke.rye each reach their own revocation counter at a different depth -- report_out.revoked, report_out.inner.revoked, below_of(report_out).inner.revoked, below_of(report_out).inner.inner.revoked -- and revoke.rye also names revoke_refusal unqualified, since it is the rung that publishes it. Four structural differences, four bodies left whole.
think The lift: pub fn revoke_one(comptime rung: type, io: std.Io, table: *rung.Table, slot: u32, keep: u32, report_out: *rung.Report) (rung.RunError || rung.NoteError)!void, reaching revoke_rung, revoke, confirm_pruned, and abandoning_of through the rung and cycle.max_hops in the harness.
think Every meter moved in the same lap as the fold: the carry ceiling to 67,363, the sink corpus to 64,939, farewell.rye's holding to 3,841, and the reach witness repointed from revoke_one to judge_outcome so the queue head stays asserted rather than recited.
obs The corrected fall formula predicted 468 and the carry fell exactly 468: 67,831 to 67,363. Three exact hits in a row now -- 492, 528, 468 -- across families of forty-two, twelve, and forty rungs.
obs A sweep of my own rewrote the body it had just written. The stub loop grepped for the string "pub fn revoke_one" and caravan/ladder_checks.rye had, one command earlier, become a file containing exactly that string -- so the harness stubbed itself into calling itself. The build refused with an undeclared identifier on the first run and the body was restored. The transferable rule: a sweep keyed on the signature a lift publishes will match the lift, so a sweep must exclude the file it is folding into, by name.
obs Checked before booking a row, and the row was already booked: tools/ladder_stub_length_scan.sh names this exact shape -- "a lift's stub loop swept the harness in with its rungs" -- and refuses it as harness_delegates_to_itself, standing since REDS %128 and %132 and riding the era suite as rung ten. The loom exists; I reached for a build rather than for the guard that was built for this. Recording the recurrence honestly rather than booking a fourth row that would teach nothing new, and naming the faster instrument: run the stub-length guard immediately after a sweep, before the build.
obs Two folds in one round, both free of the only cost that was ever real, and neither one free by accident: each was priced by reading its private symbols against the harness's own imports before a line moved. The reading the split widening column opened is holding across four consecutive families.
obs The next head is judge_outcome at four hundred and sixty-eight, thirty-seven rungs whose thirty-seven widenings all bind carry, with door_admits at four hundred and sixty-two binding system. The harness imports both, so both are free on the same reading; twenty-six of judge_outcome's sixty-three declarations differ, which is the largest divergent cohort the arc has yet met and wants reading before lifting.
